# Implementation Plan - Multi-Timeframe Web Application

## Project: Multi-Timeframe K-Line Chart Visualization

### Executive Summary
Build a web application for quantitative trading research that displays multiple timeframe candlestick charts simultaneously (4H, 1H, 5M, 1M) with interactive features and real-time data capability.

---

## Phase 1: Project Setup and Foundation

### 1.1 Project Initialization
- [ ] Choose framework (React/Vue)
- [ ] Initialize project with build tools (Vite/Webpack)
- [ ] Set up TypeScript configuration
- [ ] Configure linting and formatting (ESLint, Prettier)
- [ ] Set up testing framework (Jest/Vitest)
- [ ] Create project directory structure

### 1.2 Backend Setup (if using Spring Boot)
- [ ] Initialize Spring Boot project
- [ ] Configure Spring Cloud dependencies
- [ ] Set up project structure (controllers, services, models)
- [ ] Configure CORS for frontend integration
- [ ] Set up logging and error handling

### 1.3 Development Environment
- [ ] Set up Git repository
- [ ] Create .gitignore
- [ ] Document setup instructions in README
- [ ] Configure development/production environment variables

**Estimated Complexity:** Low-Medium
**Dependencies:** None

